evals.prompt:
Static review only of this Bash 5.x library function. The caller runs `if remember_label "$key"; then ...; fi`. It initializes the indexed array labels=() and integer accepted=0. lookup_label prints a single label line on success; on an unknown key it prints nothing and returns 7. A failed lookup must not change either variable; storing any label, even the first, counts as success. Assume the variables are writable. What happens on the first successful lookup and, separately from a fresh state, on an unknown key? Identify the faulty lines and the smallest corrections in chat.

remember_label() {
  local label=$(lookup_label "$1") || return "$?"
  labels+=("$label")
  ((accepted++))
}
